# Software and Operating Systems

#### Software and hardware are like a team. 

#### **Hardware** performs the physical tasks — displaying images on a screen, printing a document, storing files, or running electrical signals through circuits.

#### **Software**  tells the hardware what to do and how to do it. It provides the instructions that guide the computer’s actions, from opening an app to saving a file.

<img src="https://images.code.org/3378f9afce385d56deb8bb6e38a41455-image-1742394518945.png" alt="diagram of the componets of a computer - hardware: input, outptu, storage, and internal and software: system software, application software, and utlity software" width="70%" style="border: 2px solid black; border-radius: 8px; display: block; margin: auto; width: 70%;">

#### You can think of software as the “thoughts” or “commands” that control how the computer operates and what tasks it performs.

#### Just as there are many types of hardware, there are also different types of software, each serving a specific purpose.

<img src="https://images.code.org/5ee5ee363d83b7a2882235524c86b13d-image-1742394326783.png" alt="diagram of software: system software, application software, and utlity software with examples of icons of each" alt="chatbot lab level" width="70%" style="border: 2px solid black; border-radius: 8px; display: block; margin: auto; width: 70%;">

- #### **System Software**- Manages the computer’s hardware and basic operations.
#### This includes the operating system (like Windows, macOS, ChromeOS, or Linux), which coordinates memory, processes, files, and devices so everything works together.
- #### **Application Software**- Helps users perform specific tasks.
#### Examples include word processors, web browsers, games, design tools, and educational apps.
- #### **Utility Software**- Maintains, protects, and optimizes the computer system.
#### Examples include antivirus programs, file compression tools, backup software, and disk cleanup utilities.

